{
  "summary": "This experiment isolated the RNA encoder effect by replacing PCA-2000 with scvi_n200 while holding all other settings (RNA-only, single profile, no fusion) constant relative to the llm_summary_001 baseline, yielding a validation accuracy of 0.520 (F1 0.498) versus 0.485 (F1 0.464) for PCA-2000. Because only the encoder changed, this single-variable comparison indicates that a learned non-linear representation captures structure that PCA-2000 misses, but the ~3.5-point gain is moderate rather than transformative, suggesting the RNA representation is a contributing but not dominant bottleneck. It remains uncertain whether further encoder exploration (e.g., scgpt) would yield larger gains, whether the improvement plateaus within the RNA-only regime, or whether multiprofile aggregation and multimodal fusion (with the image modality at 0.208 accuracy in llm_summary_002) could unlock substantially higher performance."
}

